{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2155-02-22 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. Can you tell me about what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2155-02-22 16:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi. I’ve had this pain in my upper belly for two days now. It’s the same kind I get with my pancreatitis—fullness, radiating to my back. I’ve been nauseous and throwing up, haven’t kept anything down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2155-02-22 16:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Any fever, cough, or urinary symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2155-02-22 16:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no fever or anything like that. Just the pain and nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2155-02-22 16:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. We know you have chronic pancreatitis from your CF gene mutation, and you usually don’t have high lipase during flares. We’ll treat this as an acute flare. We’ve started IV fluids and Dilaudid for pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2155-02-22 16:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. That last dose already helped a little."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2155-02-22 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your labs. Your lipase is 50, which is normal, but that fits your history. Liver enzymes are a bit high, but not alarming. We’ll keep you NPO for now and give nutrition through the IV."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2155-02-22 17:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I usually can’t eat during these flares."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2155-02-23 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How’s the pain today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2155-02-23 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still there, but better than yesterday. Still nauseous though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2155-02-23 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep the IV anti-nausea meds going. Also, you mentioned a headache—any idea what kind it is?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2155-02-23 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Feels like my usual migraines. I’ve taken Fioricet before, even when I’m NPO."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2155-02-23 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, we’ll give you Fioricet every four hours as needed. We’ll also keep monitoring your heart with EKGs since you’re on Seroquel and amitriptyline."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2155-02-23 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Wait, is that because of the long QT issue last time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2155-02-23 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Your QTc was 440 on admission—within normal, but we’re cautious. We’ll recheck it after restarting your meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2155-02-24 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your pain is improving. We’re going to try advancing your diet to clear liquids today if you’re up for it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2155-02-24 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. I’d love to try something small."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2155-02-24 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start slow. Also, we’re restarting your home meds—Lisinopril, amlodipine, omeprazole, and Lamictal—since you’re tolerating PO."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2155-02-24 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And Seroquel and amitriptyline?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2155-02-24 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll restart those today too, but we’ll monitor your EKG closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2155-02-25 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re switching from IV Dilaudid to your oral tramadol for pain control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2155-02-25 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I prefer the tramadol anyway."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2155-02-25 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, we noticed a sore on your lower gum. Is that from biting it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2155-02-25 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I must’ve bitten it when I was dry heaving. It’s pretty painful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2155-02-25 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you lidocaine viscous mouthwash to use before meals to help with the pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2155-02-26 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re ordering a CT scan today to make sure there’s no pseudocyst or blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2155-02-26 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Last time it was clear, so I hope this is too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2155-02-27 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The CT came back. No pseudocyst, no obstruction, no mass. Your pancreas looks normal. The colon has some changes from old colitis, but nothing new."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2155-02-27 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. So it’s just the flare?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2155-02-27 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’re confident it’s acute on chronic pancreatitis. We’ll keep advancing your diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2155-02-28 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to place a midline in your right arm today. Your veins have been tough to access, and this will help with fluids and meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2155-02-28 09:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that like a PICC line?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2155-02-28 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Similar, but shorter and doesn’t go as far. It’s safer given your history of clots in the left arm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2155-02-28 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The midline was placed successfully in your right brachial vein. It’s working well, and you’re already getting fluids through it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2155-02-28 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I hope this helps avoid more needle sticks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2155-03-01 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve been reviewing your labs. Your hemoglobin is low at 9.1, but it’s stable for you. It’s normocytic, and iron studies are normal, so it’s likely chronic underproduction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2155-03-01 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So no transfusion needed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2155-03-01 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at this time. It’s not causing symptoms, and you’re not actively bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2155-03-01 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, your EKG today shows QTc of 449. It’s slightly up from admission, but still not prolonged. We’ll follow up with your PCP to check it again soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2155-03-01 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I stop Seroquel?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2155-03-01 15:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, we’ll keep it for now. But your PCP will need to check your heart function and possibly do an echo."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2155-03-02 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. You’re eating regular food, pain is controlled with oral meds, and you’re moving around fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2155-03-02 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2155-03-02 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, likely tomorrow. We’ll discharge you on your regular meds, including tramadol, Creon, and your psychiatric medications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2155-03-02 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the mouth sore?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2155-03-02 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep using the lidocaine rinse. See your dentist or PCP if it doesn’t heal in a week or two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2155-03-02 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the weight check you mentioned?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2155-03-02 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, weigh yourself daily. If you gain more than three pounds, call your doctor—could be fluid buildup."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2155-03-02 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Any restrictions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2155-03-02 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No heavy lifting with your right arm for a few days because of the midline. Otherwise, resume normal activities as tolerated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re cleared to go home today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What’s the plan after discharge?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue all your medications as prescribed. Follow up with your PCP in a week, especially for the EKG to check your QTc."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my pain specialist?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, follow up with Dr. ___ for pain management. Same for your psychiatrist and neurologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been through a lot, but I feel much better now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done really well. We’re confident you’ll continue to improve at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Call us if symptoms return or if you have any concerns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You too. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick update—your discharge papers are ready. You’ll get prescriptions for all your meds, including Creon and tramadol."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect. I’ll make sure to pick them up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, keep using the lidocaine rinse for the mouth ulcer until it heals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Any diet changes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Low-fat diet as usual. Small, frequent meals. Avoid alcohol completely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know the drill. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re all set. We’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate it. I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll have the discharge team get you ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Thanks for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care and feel better soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—your midline will be removed at your follow-up if it’s no longer needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll let them know."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And keep monitoring your weight and symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’ve learned my triggers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good to hear. Stay in touch with your care team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You too. We’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set. The nurse will assist you with discharge paperwork."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2155-03-03 07:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Get some rest."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2155-02-22 16:24:00",
    "admission_end": "2155-03-03 15:42:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient, a woman with chronic pancreatitis due to a CFTR gene mutation, cardiomyopathy, depression, anxiety, seizure disorder, and a history of venous thrombosis, was admitted for an acute exacerbation characterized by epigastric pain, nausea, and vomiting. She was managed with IV fluids, IV Dilaudid for pain, and antiemetics per protocol. A midline catheter was placed on hospital day 6 to ensure reliable venous access. Her diet was advanced as tolerated, and home medications, including Lamictal, Seroquel, and amitriptyline, were restarted once she could tolerate oral intake. She was treated for migraine headaches with Fioricet and for an aphthous ulcer with lidocaine viscous mouthwash. A CT scan showed no pseudocyst, obstruction, or mass. Her QTc interval was monitored due to psychiatric medications and remained within acceptable limits. The patient improved clinically and was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to follow up with her PCP for EKG monitoring, continue all medications, and monitor her weight for fluid retention.",
    "problems": [
      "Other acute pancreatitis",
      "Other chronic pancreatitis",
      "Epigastric pain",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Migraine, unspecified, not intractable, without status migrainosus",
      "Recurrent oral aphthae",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Cardiomyopathy, unspecified",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "Sedative, hypnotic or anxiolytic dependence with withdrawal, unspecified",
      "Other psychoactive substance dependence, uncomplicated",
      "Personal history of self-harm",
      "Personal history of other venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Cystic fibrosis carrier",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Vitamin D deficiency, unspecified",
      "Epilepsy, unspecified, not intractable, without status epilepticus"
    ]
  }
}
